{"hypotheses":[
  {"statement":"Beverage revenue is high primarily because a small set of products dominate sales, not broad-based demand across the menu.","priorConfidence":0.55,"target":"beverage_revenue_by_product","action":"breakdown","expectation":"A few product_name values account for a disproportionate share (e.g., top 2-3 products >50%) of drink_revenue; if revenue is evenly spread across many products, this is refuted."},
  {"statement":"High beverage revenue is driven by a specific customer_type (e.g., one segment ordering disproportionately more drinks) rather than uniform demand across customer types.","priorConfidence":0.5,"target":"customer_profile","action":"breakdown","expectation":"drink_revenue or drink_revenue_pct differs sharply across customer_type segments, with one segment contributing a majority share; near-equal distribution refutes this."},
  {"statement":"Beverage revenue is concentrated among a small group of repeat top customers rather than broad customer participation.","priorConfidence":0.45,"target":"top_beverage_customers","action":"lookup_block","expectation":"The top customers list shows a steep drop-off (top few customers contribute a large % of total drink revenue); a flat/long-tail distribution refutes this."},
  {"statement":"Beverage revenue is high mainly because of rising order volume (more drink_orders) rather than higher revenue per order.","priorConfidence":0.4,"target":"orders.drink_orders","action":"compare_time","expectation":"drink_orders count grows in proportion to drink_revenue over time; if drink_revenue grows faster than order count, this is refuted in favor of price/mix effects."},
  {"statement":"The high beverage revenue reflects a recent month-over-month growth spike rather than a sustained structural pattern.","priorConfidence":0.35,"target":"order_item.revenue_growth_mom","action":"compare_time","expectation":"revenue_growth_mom for drink revenue shows a sharp recent uptick concentrated in one or two months; a steady, consistent growth rate across months refutes this."}
]}
